# Line endings are a property of the FILE TYPE here, not of the machine that
# happens to check it out.
#
# Added 2026-10-28. `*.bat` files are executed by cmd.exe, which does not
# reliably honour a bare LF. The live launcher
# `13_COMMAND_CENTER/bat/sentinel-cc.bat` came back with 104 bare LF after the
# working tree was replaced from another copy on 2026-10-28 13:09 - a rewrite
# that bypassed git, so git's checkout never converted it.
#
# The blob in git was LF all along, which is correct: git stores LF and
# converts on checkout. `core.autocrlf=true` was set in this repository, so a
# normal checkout produced the CRLF cmd.exe needs and the defect stayed
# invisible for as long as every tree came out of git. A clone on a machine
# with `core.autocrlf=false` would have produced the same LF file - the
# conversion was never stated in the repository, only in a machine-local
# setting.
#
# `text eol=crlf` states it in the repository: the blob stays LF (this rule
# does not rewrite history and does not change any stored content) and every
# checkout, on every machine, produces the CRLF that cmd.exe needs.
#
# Only `.bat` is listed. `.ps1` and `.py` read LF perfectly well, and a rule
# that normalises files which are already correct is churn for its own sake.
*.bat text eol=crlf
